NAME
    mem - hexdump a range of memory

SYNOPSIS
    mem <space> <addr> [<len>]

DESCRIPTION
    Prints <len> bytes (default 16) from memory space <space> starting at
    <addr> as a 16-byte-per-row hexadecimal and printable-ASCII dump.
    <space> is a name listed by spaces(1). Both <addr> and <len> are
    parsed as hexadecimal (optional '0x' or '$' prefix accepted).

EXAMPLES
    mem WRAM 0
    mem CpuBus 8000 64

EXIT STATUS
    0   Memory dumped (or usage message printed).
    1   No target attached, unknown space, invalid hex argument, or
        session service fault.

SEE ALSO
    spaces(1), write(1), dump(1), load(1), memfind(1), addr(1)
